{"id":"m1-02-s2","title":"Stage 2: Chirp at 1k users","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: separate DB host, connection pool sizing, indexes, slow query log, basic monitoring. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"load-and-goal","title":"Load and goal","html":"<p><strong>Stage 2: about 1,000 users.</strong> Chirp now has a real audience. Goal: stop the database and app from hurting each other, make queries fast, and be able to see what is going on.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 1,000 users, 30% active daily = 300 DAU. Each loads the timeline 15 times and posts 1 time: 300 x 16 = 4,800 requests a day, about 0.06 requests/s on average; peak 10x (evening) is about 0.6 requests/s. Data: 300 posts a day x 365 = about 110k posts a year, a few tens of MB. This is still tiny, so the problems are not volume but <strong>contention</strong> (app and DB on one VM) and <strong>blindness</strong> (no idea which query is slow).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 594 130\" width=\"594\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stage 2: database moves to its own host\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 65 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 65 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 65 L450 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 65 L450 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Users</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Nginx</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Chirp app</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"516\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">RDS Postgres</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"516\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Disk for images</text></svg><figcaption>Stage 2: database moves to its own host</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Nearly every product ends up separating app and DB first; it is the cheapest scaling step. GitHub and Shopify ran large MySQL boxes for years before any sharding.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The cook and the pantry sharing one tiny kitchen. Moving the pantry next door gives the cook elbow room.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thinking 1,000 users needs a cluster. It needs a separate, backed-up database and an index.</li>\n<li>Giving no numbers. 0.06 requests/s is the honest answer; say it, then say why you still split.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"configuration","title":"Configuration","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Value</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>App VM</td>\n<td><code>t3.medium</code> (2 vCPU, 4 GB), JVM <code>-Xmx2g</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Database</td>\n<td>RDS PostgreSQL 16, <code>db.t4g.medium</code> (2 vCPU, 4 GB), 50 GB gp3, <strong>Multi-AZ off</strong> (see cost), automated backups 7 days, PITR on</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Same region, same AZ as app</td>\n<td>Round-trip latency under 1 ms</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>HikariCP</td>\n<td><code>maximumPoolSize=10</code>, <code>minimumIdle=5</code>, <code>connectionTimeout=3000</code>, <code>idleTimeout=600000</code>, <code>maxLifetime=1740000</code> (29 min, below any firewall/LB idle kill)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Postgres</td>\n<td><code>max_connections=100</code> (RDS default scales with RAM), <code>shared_buffers=1GB</code>, <code>effective_cache_size=3GB</code>, <code>work_mem=8MB</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Slow query log</td>\n<td><code>log_min_duration_statement=200</code>, <code>pg_stat_statements</code> enabled, <code>auto_explain.log_min_duration=500</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monitoring</td>\n<td>CloudWatch metrics + alarms, Grafana Cloud free tier via Prometheus scrape of Spring Boot <code>/actuator/prometheus</code>, uptime ping every 1 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Backups</td>\n<td>RDS automated daily snapshot + continuous WAL (PITR), RPO about 5 min</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>HikariCP settings in <code>application.yml</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">spring</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  datasource</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    url</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">jdbc:postgresql://chirp-db.xxxx.rds.amazonaws.com:5432/chirp</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    hikari</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      maximum-pool-size</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">10</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      minimum-idle</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      connection-timeout</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">3000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">      # fail fast instead of piling up threads</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      max-lifetime</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1740000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">      leak-detection-threshold</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">20000</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Setting <code>maxLifetime</code> longer than the network idle timeout; you get \"connection reset\" errors once an hour.</li>\n<li>Forgetting <code>connectionTimeout</code>; threads wait forever and a DB blip becomes a full app outage.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-and-why","title":"Decision and why","html":"<p><strong>Decision 1: managed DB (RDS) vs self-managed Postgres on another VM.</strong> Options: (a) second EC2 with Postgres you patch and back up yourself, (b) RDS. Chosen: RDS. For +$30 a month you get automated backups, point-in-time recovery, one-click minor upgrades and a path to Multi-AZ and replicas. Cost of an engineer's evening spent on a failed restore is higher.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 2: pool size.</strong> A common rule of thumb (from the HikariCP pool-sizing notes, derived from PostgreSQL's own guidance): <code>connections = (core_count x 2) + effective_spindle_count</code>. The DB has 2 cores, so about 5 to 10. We pick 10 per app instance. Why a <em>small</em> pool is faster: a DB core can only run one query at a time; 100 connections just queue inside Postgres and add context switching. Important maths for later: <code>total = pool_size x app_instances</code> must stay well under <code>max_connections</code>, minus reserved ones for admin.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 3: indexes.</strong> Indexes chosen from the slow query log, not guesswork.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- timeline: posts by author, newest first</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> INDEX</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> CONCURRENTLY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> posts_author_created </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">ON</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> posts (author_id, created_at </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">DESC</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- who follows me (fan-out and counts)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> INDEX</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> CONCURRENTLY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> follows_followee </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">ON</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> follows (followee_id, follower_id);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- notifications inbox</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">CREATE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> INDEX</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> CONCURRENTLY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> notif_user_unread </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">ON</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> notifications (user_id, created_at </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">DESC</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">WHERE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> read_at </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">IS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> NULL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><code>CONCURRENTLY</code> avoids locking writes during the build. The partial index only stores unread rows, so it stays small.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision 4: what to monitor first.</strong> The four golden signals: latency (p50/p95/p99), traffic (requests/s), errors (5xx rate), saturation (CPU, DB connections, free memory, disk IOPS).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 634.8 68\" width=\"634.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Find, explain, fix a slow query\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M136.8 34 L192.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M324.8 34 L380.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M470.8 34 L526.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M470.8 34 L526.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"74.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Slow query log</text><rect x=\"192.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"258.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">EXPLAIN ANALYZE</text><rect x=\"380.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"425.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Add index</text><rect x=\"526.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"574.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Re-measure</text></svg><figcaption>Find, explain, fix a slow query</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> GitHub and Uber publish that most early performance wins were missing indexes and N+1 queries. Instagram engineers used <code>pg_stat_statements</code> to find top queries by total time. Percona and pganalyze build whole products around the slow log.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The index at the back of a book: instead of reading every page to find \"Postgres\", you jump to page 212.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"add an index on every column\". Each index slows writes and uses RAM.</li>\n<li>Index column order: <code>(author_id, created_at DESC)</code> serves \"posts by author, newest first\"; reversed it does not.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"alternatives-branches","title":"Alternatives (branches)","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Choice</th>\n<th>Option A</th>\n<th>Option B</th>\n<th>Verdict</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Database host</td>\n<td>RDS</td>\n<td>EC2 self-managed</td>\n<td>RDS now; self-managed only if cost at scale dominates (e.g. Instagram, Notion later run their own)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Aurora PostgreSQL</td>\n<td>Better storage layer, up to 15 replicas</td>\n<td>About 20% more cost, vendor lock-in</td>\n<td>Not yet; reconsider at Stage 4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pooler</td>\n<td>App-side HikariCP only</td>\n<td>PgBouncer in front</td>\n<td>HikariCP only for one app VM; PgBouncer needed once app instances x pool exceed limits (Stage 3 to 4)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monitoring</td>\n<td>CloudWatch + Grafana Cloud</td>\n<td>Datadog / New Relic</td>\n<td>Free tiers now; paid APM when team grows</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-AZ</td>\n<td>Off (about $60)</td>\n<td>On (about $120)</td>\n<td>Off now (RPO 5 min via PITR is acceptable at 1k users); turn on before Stage 3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 448 130\" width=\"448\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where to put connection pooling\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 96 L346 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 96 L346 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">HikariCP in app</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">PgBouncer</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"391\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres</text></svg><figcaption>Where to put connection pooling</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying PgBouncer is mandatory. It matters when many instances (or serverless) open many connections.</li>\n<li>Treating RDS Multi-AZ as a backup. It is failover; it replicates mistakes too.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-breaks-next","title":"What breaks next","html":"<ol>\n<li><strong>A single app VM</strong> is a single point of failure and every deploy drops traffic. Symptom: uptime ping red for 15 s on every release.</li>\n<li><strong>Single DB host without a standby</strong> (Multi-AZ off): an AZ failure means manual restore, RTO about 30 min.</li>\n<li><strong>Local-disk images</strong> cannot be shared by a second app server.</li>\n<li><strong>Sessions in memory</strong> (cookie to server session) break the moment there are two servers.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Metric to watch: p95 latency above 300 ms, DB CPU above 60% sustained, <code>HikariPool pending threads</code> above 0 for minutes, free disk below 20%.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 748.8000000000001 68\" width=\"748.8000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stage 2 to Stage 3 pressure\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M563.2 34 L619.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M563.2 34 L619.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">One app VM</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"258.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Single point of failure</text><rect x=\"409.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"486.40000000000003\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Add 2nd app server</text><rect x=\"619.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"678\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text></svg><figcaption>Stage 2 to Stage 3 pressure</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Declaring victory because latency is good now. A single instance has no availability story.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"cost","title":"Cost","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Item</th>\n<th>Monthly</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>App <code>t3.medium</code></td>\n<td>about $30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RDS <code>db.t4g.medium</code> single-AZ</td>\n<td>about $60</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>50 GB gp3 for DB</td>\n<td>about $6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Backup storage (7 days)</td>\n<td>about $3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>EBS for app + media</td>\n<td>about $5</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Monitoring (free tier)</td>\n<td>$0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Data transfer, DNS, misc</td>\n<td>about $10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>about $115 per month</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>If Multi-AZ is turned on: about $175 per month. At 1,000 users that is about $0.12 to $0.18 per user per month.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Overlooking that Multi-AZ doubles the DB price.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"lld-view","title":"LLD view","html":"<p>Same layers as Stage 1, with two new technical seams.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Controller -> Service -> Repository -> HikariCP pool -> RDS</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                              |</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                    (query timeouts, metrics)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Micrometer timers around each repository call -> /actuator/prometheus</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Concrete code changes:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// 1. Timeouts so a slow query cannot hold a pool connection forever</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">@Query</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">@QueryHints</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">QueryHint</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(name </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"jakarta.persistence.query.timeout\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">value</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"3000\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">fun</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> timeline</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">..</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.): </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">List</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Post</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// 2. Keyset (cursor) pagination instead of OFFSET, which gets slower with depth</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// WHERE (created_at, id) &#x3C; (:ts, :id) ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC LIMIT 50</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Why keyset pagination.</strong> <code>OFFSET 10000</code> makes Postgres read and discard 10,000 rows; keyset pagination uses the index and costs the same on page 1 and page 1,000.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 564 130\" width=\"564\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Request with a timeout and metric at every hop\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 65 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 65 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M254 65 L310 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M254 65 L310 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M406 65 L462 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M406 65 L462 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M406 65 L462 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M406 65 L462 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Controller</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Service</text><rect x=\"310\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"358\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Repository</text><rect x=\"462\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"507\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">RDS</text><rect x=\"462\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"507\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Metrics</text></svg><figcaption>Request with a timeout and metric at every hop</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter and Instagram APIs expose cursors (<code>max_id</code>, <code>next_cursor</code>), not page numbers, for exactly this reason.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using <code>OFFSET/LIMIT</code> for infinite scroll.</li>\n<li>Leaving the default JDBC statement timeout at \"infinite\".</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-gravity","title":"Decision gravity","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decision</th>\n<th>Gravity</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Move DB to RDS</td>\n<td>Reversible with effort</td>\n<td><code>pg_dump</code>/logical replication can move to any Postgres; downtime minutes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pool size 10</td>\n<td>Reversible (config)</td>\n<td>Change and redeploy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Indexes</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td><code>DROP INDEX</code>; just pay build cost on big tables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-AZ on/off</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Toggle, brief failover blip</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cursor pagination in the API contract</td>\n<td><strong>One-way door for public clients</strong></td>\n<td>Once mobile apps depend on <code>offset</code>, changing it needs API versioning; choose cursors now</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Choosing RDS vs Aurora</td>\n<td>Mostly one-way</td>\n<td>Aurora storage is proprietary; leaving it needs a logical migration</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Treating the API contract as an internal detail. Published APIs are one-way doors.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"concepts-learned","title":"Concepts learned","html":"<ul>\n<li>Connection pooling and pool sizing maths; <code>pool x instances &#x3C; max_connections</code>.</li>\n<li>B-tree indexes, composite order, partial indexes, <code>CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY</code>.</li>\n<li><code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code>, slow query log, <code>pg_stat_statements</code>.</li>\n<li>Golden signals and the first alarms.</li>\n<li>Keyset vs offset pagination.</li>\n<li>PITR vs Multi-AZ: backup vs failover are different.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing up RPO (data you can lose) and RTO (time to recover).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Stage 2 (about 1k users): app <code>t3.medium</code> + RDS Postgres <code>db.t4g.medium</code>; about $115 per month.</li>\n<li>Separate DB so app and DB stop competing for RAM; gain managed backups and PITR (RPO about 5 min).</li>\n<li>Pool: HikariCP 10 connections per instance, <code>connectionTimeout</code> 3 s, <code>maxLifetime</code> 29 min.</li>\n<li>Indexes driven by <code>pg_stat_statements</code> and a 200 ms slow log; keyset pagination for the timeline.</li>\n<li>Monitor latency, traffic, errors, saturation from day one.</li>\n<li>Next bottleneck: one app server is a single point of failure and cannot be deployed without downtime, so Stage 3 goes horizontal.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}